{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1509294-favorite-convenats","id":1509294,"title":"Favorite Convenats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-22T09:40:00-07:00","id":1509294,"title":"Favorite Convenats?","content":"Myself I like the Circle Of The Crone &amp; Carthian Movement myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T10:00:54-07:00","id":1509296,"title":"","content":"I like the Lancea et Sanctum. The idea that vampires would develop a religion that self-justifies their own existence is a clever bit of world-building. Same goes for the Circle, though it's approach is maybe a bit more obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T11:28:35-07:00","id":1509305,"title":"","content":"I always liked the Cult of Augurs and the Weihan Cynn the most, both of which are, unfortunately, broken in modern times. I assume that my favorite modern covenant would be the Invictus, blood oaths are cool and the world of the CofD needs order :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T13:46:15-07:00","id":1509312,"title":"","content":"Carthians, Circle of the Crone, Tenth Choir, and Ume House.<br /> <br /> The Carthians are the most politically correct covenant, Carthian Law slaps, and are the most efficient Covenant if you want to &quot;multiclass&quot; Covenants and are willing to play into the associated role.<br /> THe Circle of the Crone are the most philosophically correct covenant, Cruac slaps, and honestly, for me, it's the most dynamic Covenant to be in, with a lot of it's tenets and traits actually playing against each other on the whole, and being a bunch of different small scale pagan cults in the same way the Carthians are a bunch of political movements doubles that.<br /> The Tenth Choir did nothing wrong. Also Therion slaps.<br /> And Ume House, particularly with Kigan(which slaps) instead of Cruac, is that perfect hybrid of vampires, magic priests, and weeby interest.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T13:46:37-07:00","id":1509313,"title":"","content":"I have grown a soft spot for the Invictus, particularly because Oaths are a cool system of powers that have a lot of mysterious crossover potential both within Requiem (different side of the same coin as Carthian Laws?) and for Changeling, but also because the First Estate is notably versatile in their aesthetics, presentation, and modes of operation - they effectively combine the 'upholders of status quo' schtick of OWoD's Ventrue with the 'adapt or die' schtick of the Lasombra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T17:17:10-07:00","id":1509329,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit surprised my favorites, the Ordo Dracul, hasn't been mentioned yet, Maybe it is a bit too mystic and weird to be a universally liked covenant?<br /> <br /> Seen it fairly often among players, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T20:21:19-07:00","id":1509344,"title":"","content":"Ordo Dracul is also my favorite. The idea of Kindred trying to transcend the curse and become something completely different is something that I find interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1494-deranged-goblin","name":"Deranged Goblin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T22:41:22-07:00","id":1509349,"title":"","content":"Ordo Dracul, because the Mysteries of the Dragon are cool as hell, and because they're the only covenant that has a set of ornate titles with secret meanings to memorize, including the most elaborate and impressive-sounding title of the set, whose secret meaning is &quot;the guy who gave me this title wants you to kill me.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think from a game design standpoint their Therion is a little unwieldy, but I have a soft spot for the Tenth Choir's sheer gall.<br /> <br /> I like the thoroughness of the consideration put to the Lancea et Sanctum and how <i>different</i> a religion for vampires would look. It doesn't always commit as far as I'd like, but it's a good springboard for some profoundly disturbing monsters.<br /> <br /> I like the Sun-Walking Knights. When I'm dealing with vampiric conspiracies, I like to lean on them, as an illustration of how temporal power co-opts. The vampires don't own the President, but the President owns several vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T00:02:48-07:00","id":1509352,"title":"","content":"Would it be cheating if I said the Camarilla ?<br /> <br /> Every wing is just jam-packed with story-potential. A (kind of) functoning unified society of literal predators. What made me love it is the mood of RFR. Everything just feels so dangerous and creepy. Monsters acting as &quot;civilised&quot; or &quot;noble&quot; beings, always at the brink of frenzy, fearing to tear into their political opponents. Fear of it not because it would be a monstrous act but because it would make you lesser in the eyes of your peers.<br /> <br /> I even love the notion of the Invictus and Carthians both claiming to be the spiritual heirs of the Camarilla but only because nobody knows the truth of the real thing.<br /> <br /> I guess I am gushing more about Requiem for Rome than the Camarilla itself but they are inseperable to me.<br /> <br /> I adore everything about RFR. It is what got first me into VTR and everything about it is just kickass to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T00:04:55-07:00","id":1509353,"title":"","content":"From the core covenants, I really like how similar the Ordo Dracul is to the SCP foundation, especially with their focus on Wyrm's Nests. They're a way to crack into the supernatural horror of the setting; not like the contagion chronicle, but in something like a classic horror story, where you don't see the monster until it's too late.<br /> <br /> That being said, I <i>really</i> wish non-core covenants got more love. Sometimes it feels like canon doesn't want to acknowledge the idea of covenants existing outside the main five (looking at you, SotC). Among them, the Brides of Dracula stand out for reveling in vampirism in a way the other covenants don't (save the Circle).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26974-dreamwave","name":"Dreamwave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T10:22:22-07:00","id":1509392,"title":"","content":"Maybe because Ordo Dracul is a hard to portray in a game. I like the idea of a covenant wanting to move beyond the curse and all that implies and worthy of pursuit. But the drive behind it might be more then most kindred or people could do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T13:27:52-07:00","id":1509407,"title":"","content":"Belial's Brood (The 2E version) are some of my favorite antagonists in the entirety of Vampire for being peerless monsters devoid of any compassion or mercy. They also feel like a refinement of the &quot;Mindless Beast/Careful Predators&quot; divide first edition introduced.<br /> <br /> While they're not my outright favorites, I also like the Ahl al-Mumit and the Weihan Cynn for showing me ways you can have covenants based around Abrahamic and 'Pagan' faiths that aren't the Lancea Sanctum or the Circle of the Crone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12220-dark-lord-potato","name":"Dark Lord Potato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T15:55:23-07:00","id":1509413,"title":"","content":"I prefer the original Belial's Brood, with their disparate goals and beliefs, such as thinking the Antichrist has already come and left a (Mortal) bloodline.<br /> <br /> I suppose they're too similar to how the mainstream Covenants are portrayed now, but I miss them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T07:47:16-07:00","id":1509477,"title":"","content":"The Carthians, for being the best and the worst of almost every political ideology, for Carthian Law being a cool concept, and for being a viable alternative to the Invictus when creating a city. Plus they're one of only two core covenants to not get blood magic. It's like the writers looked at VtM, thought 'how can we make the Brujah even better', and then rolled eleven successes.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone and Ordo Dracul come in a joint second place for me, they're cool, have fun powers, and explore the vampiric condition. But they don't capture my imagination in the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T18:34:38-07:00","id":1509540,"title":"","content":"Of the core covenants, the Circle of the Crone, followed by the Ordo Dracul. I like the more mystical approach they take to their undead existences.<br /> Outside the big five, the Tenth Choir is cool, and the Children's Crusade is delightfully creepy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27841,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27841-haintbleu","user":"HaintBleu","date":". 04-25-2023, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27841-haintbleu","name":"HaintBleu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T19:40:39-07:00","id":1509546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1509294-favorite-convenats?p=1509413#post1509413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer the original Belial's Brood, with their disparate goals and beliefs, such as thinking the Antichrist has already come and left a (Mortal) bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lucifuge\" target=\"_blank\">Oh, really</a>? Who would have thought <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/L%27Enfants_Diabolique\" target=\"_blank\">of that</a>....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1509294-favorite-convenats?p=1509413#post1509413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose they're too similar to how the mainstream Covenants are portrayed now, but I miss them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Must admit that i'm still somewhat out of synch with how did the covenants change between editions (except for the Crone becoming more chthonic &amp; focused in its mythology instead of an umbrella for kindred polytheism as a whole) to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-07-2023, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T03:27:11-07:00","id":1509570,"title":"","content":"I still think that a lot of the gnostic theology of the 1e Brood would fit nicely with the Tenth Choir, but that's just my take on it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T20:25:55-07:00","id":1510953,"title":"","content":"Circle of the crone is cool for some of its cults<br /> <br /> Invictus is also good for when you want pageantry","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T11:36:49-07:00","id":1511079,"title":"","content":"Big fan of the Ordo Dracul, because I love me some mad scientists, and vampire mad scientists are even better. I also like the Invictus, because I think vampire politics are tons of fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27217-skyewards","name":"Skyewards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T04:44:54-07:00","id":1511343,"title":"","content":"I can find a reason to play any Covenant but one, although I think my favorite ones would probably be: Lancea and Ordo, as these are somehow the opposite in ideology.<br /> About the former I like the religious fanaticism and how they justify and embrace their monstruos nature, of the latter I like the scientific/massonic flavor they have.<br /> <br /> Chartian is the one I like the less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T16:26:29-07:00","id":1513581,"title":"","content":"Lancea Sanctum, because they are creepy and broken. <br /> <br /> The Commonwealth, because they have those towns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Organizer for the Dead Gamers Society: The So Cal World of Darkness Meetup. </span><a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/85-drumheller","name":"Drumheller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar85_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T06:50:26-07:00","id":1513642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drumheller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1509294-favorite-convenats?p=1513581#post1513581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lancea Sanctum, because they are creepy and broken.<br /> <br /> The Commonwealth, because they have those towns.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the Commonwealth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T08:30:18-07:00","id":1513649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1509294-favorite-convenats?p=1513642#post1513642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the Commonwealth?</div> </div> </div> </div>A tier three exaggeration of the Carthian Movement presented in The Danse Macabre, reimagined as having enough members and organization to take control of enough land and people to put plans of vampire-friendly future societies into motion in microcosm, and not enough foresight and control to get in front of the terrible things that can go wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T05:49:29-07:00","id":1524095,"title":"","content":"Ordo all the way, with Invictus being a clear second place. Just love the changes, (pseudo)science-y vibes, alchemical transcendance themes etc. Barring that, the Invictus seems the most interesting to me, what with the rank-climbing and backstabbing cut-throat politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T08:38:10-07:00","id":1524099,"title":"","content":"I always find myself finding things I like and dislike about most of the covenants.<br /> <br /> Tenth Choir drives me nuts trying to figure out what choir is what how the angels fit in, etc. I really wish they didn't have the Christian angle and were just about eating spirits and becoming pagan gods. If it had went that route it would be my favorite by a lot I think. As is I really enjoy therion I just think it's too complicated and don't like the exclusively monotheistic angle.<br /> <br /> I like the Ordo Dracul's desire to ascend beyond vampirism and I like several coils of the dragon as well. I just really don't care for the Dracula angle. Like in the thousands of years before Dracula no one thought to try and ascend past vampirism? (Other than the likewise fairly young Tenth Choir.)<br /> <br /> I like blood magic in general, and I think faith based covenants provide interesting options so I like both the Sanctum and the Circle. I think Thraban Sorcery and Cruac are both unfortunately weak in the core rules though Secrets of the Covenants and NMD help fill them out.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it really counts as liking the covenant, but since I read about members of the Appolinaire bloodline joining the Architects of the Monolith and trying to build arcane cities in the Underworld I've been fascinated by that idea. Just something about a voodoo using vampire building buildings and then destroying them to use them in the underworld is fascinating to me. It doesn't hurt that for a building to transfer over a lot of emotional energy, say like a tragedy, would be needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 10-15-2023, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T08:03:18-07:00","id":1524138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1509294-favorite-convenats?p=1524099#post1524099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the Ordo Dracul's desire to ascend beyond vampirism and I like several coils of the dragon as well. I just really don't care for the Dracula angle. Like in the thousands of years before Dracula no one thought to try and ascend past vampirism? (Other than the likewise fairly young Tenth Choir.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't see what the big deal is - Ancient Mysteries throws in the idea that some sect of undead buddhist monks might have discovered something pretty much like the coils centuries, if not millenia before Dracula. Damn, the OD book itself gives hints left and right that a number of its internal factions, study groups and cults were already doing their own niche thing before Dracula would collate ideas and bring them all together.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly possible that other kindred did experiments on similar or more bizarre lines long before and a few even formed bloodlines or covenants of their own. The Qedeshah from Bloodlines: the Hidden with its kabbalistic elements could be circunstantial evidence of the Dammitic Creed existing long before the Lancea et Sanctum.\u200b<br /> <br /> Both Requiem for Rome and Ancient Mysteries are there to show how covenants appeared and turned to dust as civilizations rose and fell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T09:34:38-07:00","id":1524140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1509294-favorite-convenats?p=1524138#post1524138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly don't see what the big deal is</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't see that your understanding is required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T12:54:46-07:00","id":1524148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1509294-favorite-convenats?p=1524140#post1524140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly don't see that your understanding is required.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pet peeves are pet peeves, fair. Anyway, as books outside the Core did adress (back in 1e even), other people <b><i>thought </i></b>to try and ascend past vampirism in the thousands of years before Dracula. He's simply the one who managed to form a large covenant of similar-minded people that is relatively familiar to <i>contemporary </i>kindred in a large part of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-16-2023, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T21:14:07-07:00","id":1524179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1509294-favorite-convenats?p=1524099#post1524099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the Ordo Dracul's desire to ascend beyond vampirism and I like several coils of the dragon as well. I just really don't care for the Dracula angle. Like in the thousands of years before Dracula no one thought to try and ascend past vampirism? (Other than the likewise fairly young Tenth Choir.)<br /> <br /> I like blood magic in general, and I think faith based covenants provide interesting options so I like both the Sanctum and the Circle. I think Thraban Sorcery and Cruac are both unfortunately weak in the core rules though Secrets of the Covenants and NMD help fill them out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Excellent point about the Ordo Dracul that always bugged me too! Vampires have been around since at least the heyday of the Roman Empire, yet it took a mass murdering torturer to go &quot;you know what I am going to look into this.&quot; Despite ancient Rome having several notable and intelligent philosophers who would think to ponder such a thing.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> What is NMD if I may ask? I am always looking for more blood magic rules rather than converting them from Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Oh! If we are trading sources, I highly recommend Blood Sorcery rites of damnation which is a 2.e update for 1.e Requiem's sacraments and blasphemies. Lots of nice spells in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T04:45:37-07:00","id":1524191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1509294-favorite-convenats?p=1524179#post1524179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Excellent point about the Ordo Dracul that always bugged me too! Vampires have been around since at least the heyday of the Roman Empire, yet it took a mass murdering torturer to go &quot;you know what I am going to look into this.&quot; Despite ancient Rome having several notable and intelligent philosophers who would think to ponder such a thing.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> What is NMD if I may ask? I am always looking for more blood magic rules rather than converting them from Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Oh! If we are trading sources, I highly recommend Blood Sorcery rites of damnation which is a 2.e update for 1.e Requiem's sacraments and blasphemies. Lots of nice spells in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>NMD is None More Dark Publishing. They put out books on the clans and various bloodline books and the update of Rome. It's done by a lot of people who used to write for Onyx Path. Chris Falco, the guy who wrote Rites of Damnation, also works for NMD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 10-17-2023, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T09:21:48-07:00","id":1524197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1509294-favorite-convenats?p=1524140#post1524140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly don't see that your understanding is required.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise, your approval of a difference of opinion is not required.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T09:57:55-07:00","id":1524199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1509294-favorite-convenats?p=1524197#post1524197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Likewise, your approval of a difference of opinion is not required.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not the one who made a huge post telling someone else their opinion was wrong, though I fail to see where you quoted them and thought to admonish them. <br /> <br /> And given that my response was literally in response to a post telling me my opinion was wrong and I depth as to why, I would say it was actually seeking my approval. <br /> <br /> You know what hasn't been sought in this thread though? Your two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T16:19:53-07:00","id":1524206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1509294-favorite-convenats?p=1524191#post1524191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> NMD is None More Dark Publishing. They put out books on the clans and various bloodline books and the update of Rome. It's done by a lot of people who used to write for Onyx Path. Chris Falco, the guy who wrote Rites of Damnation, also works for NMD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, okay geez I should have put that together I have their clan book rewrites, my bad.<br /> <br /> <hr />Back on the subject of Covenants I like the circle of the Crone, I find their blood sorcery far less limiting than the sanctum's and their ideal of not denying what they are kind of reminds me of the sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27607,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","user":"BloodyRelight","date":". 10-17-2023, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T20:46:53-07:00","id":1524305,"title":"","content":"I always liked either Circle of the Crone or Unaligned.<br /> <br /> Usually, when we did our troupe games with 1e when I was a kid, everyone was either Unaligned, Carthian, or Circle of the Crone, but we did have a couple of Lancea Sanctum characters.<br /> <br /> Our big bads were Belial's Brood and the Invictus, as well as mortal hunters and criminals, so there was a common enemy for all of our PC's from these covenants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}